Pie UI is a closed-source project. This repository publishes only the addon's
documentation, screenshots, and theme artwork. The source code is intentionally
not made public.


Why this project is closed source
---------------------------------
Pie UI renders a replacement HUD by reading the Guild Wars 2 client's memory,
which relies on reverse engineering of the game client. Publishing the source
would also publish those reverse-engineering details, so the code is kept
private.

Pie UI only reads the game's memory; it never writes to or modifies the game's
memory or code. A few actions that you trigger yourself — clicking a skill to
cast it, sending a chat message, or opening the world map or a build template
from a chat link — are carried out by sending ordinary keyboard input, or by
invoking the game client's own interface functions, to reproduce something you
could already do by hand. Pie UI does not alter game state directly, inject code
into the game, bot, or automate gameplay.


Permitted use
-------------
You may download and use the Pie UI addon free of charge, including while
streaming, recording, or making videos or other content — on monetised channels
as well as personal ones. Streamers and content creators are warmly welcome to
feature and showcase Pie UI. You may also quote or reuse this repository's
documentation, screenshots, and theme artwork when describing, reviewing, or
showcasing Pie UI, with attribution.

This permission does not let you sell Pie UI, charge others for access to it, or
bundle it into a paid product or service — see Restrictions below.


Distribution via Raidcore / Nexus
---------------------------------
The author grants Raidcore and the Nexus addon library (raidcore.gg) permission
to list, host, and distribute the Pie UI addon, unmodified and free of charge,
to end users through their platform. This permission is limited to distribution
of the addon as released by the author; it conveys no right to modify, sell, or
reverse engineer Pie UI, and does not affect any other restriction in this
licence.


Restrictions
------------
Except as expressly permitted above, you may not copy, modify, redistribute,
sell, decompile, disassemble, or otherwise reverse engineer the Pie UI software
or attempt to recover its source code, without prior written permission from the
author.


ArenaNet developer access
-------------------------
The author welcomes scrutiny from the people who make Guild Wars 2. Verified
ArenaNet employees may request read-only access to the complete source code in
order to review Pie UI's behaviour and confirm its compliance with the Guild
Wars 2 User Agreement and rules of conduct. To request access, contact the
author by opening an issue on this repository, via the contact form at
https://pie.rocks.cc/, or by having a GM contact PieOrCake.7635 in-game.
Such access is granted for review purposes only and conveys no license to use,
copy, modify, or redistribute the source code.


